A clean-room APL\360 interpreter with traditional glyphs, written in Rust from scratch. Flat arrays, floating point, the del editor, and the APL\360 system commands.

Usage: sw-apl [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -f, --file <FILE>
          Run FILE in batch mode instead of the interactive session

      --no-echo
          Do not echo input lines (with their indent) in batch mode

      --ws-size <BYTES>
          Workspace size in bytes: how much the workspace may hold before WS FULL
          
          [default: 1048576]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

MODES:
  sw-apl                 Interactive session when stdin is a terminal.
                         The prompt is six spaces; output starts in
                         column one, like an APL\360 printing terminal.
                         Up arrow recalls earlier lines for editing or
                         re-submission (history in ~/.sw-apl_history);
                         Ctrl-C cancels a line, Ctrl-D ends like )OFF.
  sw-apl -f FILE         Batch: run FILE line by line, echoing each
                         input line with the indent so the transcript
                         reads like a session. Stops at )OFF.
  sw-apl < FILE          Batch from stdin (same as -f).
  ./FILE.apl             An executable file: a leading #! line is
                         the shell's and is not read as APL. Put the
                         flags before -f, and prefer the portable
                         form #!/usr/bin/env -S sw-apl --no-echo -f.

WORKSPACE SIZE:
  A workspace holds a fixed number of bytes, and a value that will
  not fit in what is left is WS FULL. --ws-size sets it; the default
  is 1048576. What is left is reported by I-beam 22. The size is the
  session's, not the workspace's: it is not saved, so a workspace
  saved under a large size need not load under a small one.

INPUT:
  Traditional APL glyphs as Unicode. There are no keyword aliases.
  See docs/input-methods.md for Espanso and Emacs setups and
  docs/glyphs.txt for the accepted code points.

AI CODING AGENT INSTRUCTIONS:
  1. Run `sw-apl -f samples/NAME.apl` to see a transcript; every
     sample ends with )OFF so the run terminates.
  2. Pipe statements on stdin for one-off checks:
       printf '2+2\n)OFF\n' | sw-apl
  3. Use --no-echo when comparing raw output against another APL.
  4. Regression baselines live in tests/reg-rs; run
     scripts/reg.sh run -q before claiming behaviour is unchanged.
